Part 3: ETL Orchestration

Step Functions: Automates the workflow:

Lambda reads raw and curated data from S3

Runs Glue ETL jobs

Executes Athena queries

Writes results back to S3

Part 4: Query & Analytics

AWS Glue: Crawls the S3 buckets to infer schemas and maintain a metadata catalog.

Athena: Queries transformed data in S3 for analytics or reporting purposes.

Part 5: Monitoring & Alerts

CloudWatch Logs:

Captures logs for Lambda functions and Step Functions executions.

Tracks execution success, failures, and errors for debugging.

CloudWatch Alarms & SNS:

Sends email alerts if any component fails or if data volume is unexpectedly low.

Enables proactive monitoring of the ETL pipeline.
